  "body": "![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1342360/102247236-9904b980-3ef7-11eb-8ea5-a15b496d6cfb.png)\r\n\r\nI saw this random floating link about the top-level spec page and got a bit confused. Only when I clicked on another page and saw this:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1342360/102247445-e1bc7280-3ef7-11eb-92db-8e9edf946e6d.png)\r\n\r\nDid I realise what was going on.\r\n\r\nWe might want to either:\r\n\r\n* Not show breadcrumbs when there's only one item.\r\n* Show something like \"You are here: ...\" in front so it's not just a naked hyperlink.\r\n* Keep the `/` on the end if it's just one item.\r\n\r\nOr something of that nature to give context to what that actually is, especially since it'll likely be one of the first things people see :)",
